      "text": "By Vieta's formulas, $a,$ $b,$ $c$ are the roots of $3x^3 - 3x^2 + 11x - 8 = 0,$ so by Vieta's formulas, We have $abc = - \\frac{8}{3},$ $ab + ac + bc = \\frac{11}{3},$ $ab^2 + abc + a^2b = \\frac{26}{3},$ $abc^2 + abc + a^2c + b^2c + ac^2b + bc^2a = \\frac{72}{3}.$  Subtracting $ab$ and $bc,$ we get $a(ab + ac + bc) + b(ab + ac + bc) = 72 - \\frac{26}{3} - \\frac{8}{3} = \\frac{78}{3} \\implies a(b + c) + b(a + c) = \\frac{78}{3} \\cdot 3 = 78,$ so $a(b + c) + b(c + a) = a(a + b) + b(a + c) = \\boxed{26}.$ The answer is 26",
